  "description": {
   "value": "<p><strong>Category:</strong> Luxury</p>\n<p><strong>Fabrication:</strong> DV29 - 5,000eb - 1 Month</p>\n<p><strong>Eligible:</strong> All Melee Weapons</p>\n<p><em>Monoblades? Orbital crystals? Who cares when you can use nanotech serrated blades that are even deadlier than a scifi laser sword?</em></p>\n<p><strong>Iconic Weapon Mod.</strong> When dealing damage to a target in the Seriously Wounded Wound State via an Aimed Shot with the weapon, the victim suffers damage and effects as if they were instead in the Mortally Wounded Wound State (i.e., they automatically suffer a Critical Injury and their Death Save Penalty is increased by 1). When instead dealing damage via an Aimed Shot with the weapon to a target in the Mortally Wounded Wound State, instead of the user rolling on the relevant Critical Injury table, the user may select a specific Critical Injury (of the relevant location) to immediately apply to the victim.</p>\n<p><strong>Foundry notes:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Iconic: it can't be bought or sourced on the street, can't be fabricated without its Blueprint, can't be taken during Character Generation, and once acquired can't be destroyed unless the player agrees to it beforehand.</li>\n<li>The price is the Luxury benchmark, for working out repairs and Tech Upgrades. Iconics can't be bought.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><em>From <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13EnSAoiLDsC7zmL-Jr1RqIh_EnuVuFnExqiipDVquMk/edit\">Corgo's 77 Collection V3</a> by Corgopolis (Becoming Iconic &gt; Iconic Weapons).</em></p>"
  },
